cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Grisaille in research, please cite it as below."
title: "Grisaille: plan the values, generate over them, read what held"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Parrish
    given-names: Russell
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9781-7995
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: 2026-11-14
license: MIT
url: https://www.parallaxmetrology.com
repository-code: https://github.com/parallaxmetrology/grisaille
keywords: [value plan, notan, painting, controlnet, stable diffusion, inpainting, receipt, image analysis]
abstract: >
  A painter's value plan (2, 3 or 5 values) is handed to Stable Diffusion 1.5 with ControlNet 1.1,
  and the picture is read back against the plan: pattern held after one global key and contrast fit,
  exact values held, merged or swapped values, and lost shapes. Variants are ranked by that receipt,
  lost shapes can be repaired in place, and an edited plan can be repainted only where it changed.
